    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a solid start for that section. I also want to make sure I'm not missing anything crucial for my defense. Some people say that these critiques are just social constructs and that the actual psychometric data shows these tests are objectively valid and predictive of life outcomes. Is there a scientific consensus that says these critiques are actually just wrong? Or how do the proponents of these tests respond to the points you just made?",
