    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you. It sounds like you're saying the psychometric defense of these tests is pretty much debunked by the sociological reality. If someone were to argue that IQ tests are actually the most \"fair\" way to identify talent because they aren't subject to human favoritism or nepotism, would that be a logically sound argument, or is that just a fundamentally flawed way of looking at it?",
