      "content": "The argument that IQ tests are \"fair\" because they remove human bias is a logical fallacy that ignores how the tests themselves are biased by design and context. True fairness requires equal opportunity to prepare for the test, which is impossible when schools and families are systematically unequal. Relying on these tests as a \"neutral\" filter simply automates and scales existing social inequalities, making the outcome less fair, not more.",
